WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.203
<v Examiner>The male reproductive system.

2
00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:03.821
<v Examiner>Ten marks.

3
00:00:04.271 --> 00:00:09.092
<v Examiner>Label all the structures of the male reproductive system, and state their functions.

4
00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.812
This is the male half of her biggest written question:

5
00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:18.019
ten marks on her student-marked quiz, and her model answer is a link to her own notes.

6
00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:22.197
So here are her notes, organ by organ, in the order the sperm travel.

7
00:00:22.197 --> 00:00:26.011
She'll give you a side-on diagram, so picture it as you listen.

8
00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:29.163
The hook: make, store, carry, add, deliver.

9
00:00:29.163 --> 00:00:34.190
The testes make, the epididymis stores, the ducts carry, three glands add fluid,

10
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.635
and the penis delivers.

11
00:00:36.085 --> 00:00:39.775
The system's function: to produce the gametes, the sperm;

12
00:00:39.775 --> 00:00:43.272
to secrete the male sex hormones, mainly testosterone;

13
00:00:43.272 --> 00:00:47.157
and to deliver the sperm into the female reproductive tract.

14
00:00:47.607 --> 00:00:51.944
The scrotum: a skin sac outside the body cavity, holding the two testes.

15
00:00:51.944 --> 00:00:56.041
Hanging outside keeps them about three degrees cooler than the core,

16
00:00:56.041 --> 00:00:57.788
which sperm production needs.

17
00:00:57.788 --> 00:01:00.258
Two muscles hold that temperature steady.

18
00:01:00.258 --> 00:01:04.414
The dartos is smooth muscle that wrinkles the skin, to cut heat loss.

19
00:01:04.414 --> 00:01:09.836
The cremaster is skeletal muscle that pulls the testes up towards the body when it's cold.

20
00:01:10.286 --> 00:01:12.131
The testes: the male gonads.

21
00:01:12.131 --> 00:01:15.491
Inside, the seminiferous tubules produce the sperm.

22
00:01:15.491 --> 00:01:19.180
Between the tubules, the Leydig cells make testosterone.

23
00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:23.726
And the Sertoli cells nourish the developing sperm, and make inhibin.

24
00:01:25.176 --> 00:01:29.919
The epididymis: a cup-shaped duct on the back of each testis, with a head,

25
00:01:29.919 --> 00:01:31.073
a body and a tail.

26
00:01:31.073 --> 00:01:35.303
It stores the sperm, and it's where they mature and become motile.

27
00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:39.789
At ejaculation it contracts, and pushes them on into the vas deferens.

28
00:01:40.239 --> 00:01:43.322
The vas deferens, also called the ductus deferens:

29
00:01:43.322 --> 00:01:47.698
the duct that carries the sperm from the epididymis up into the pelvis,

30
00:01:47.698 --> 00:01:49.733
where it widens into the ampulla.

31
00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:54.972
A vasectomy cuts the vas deferens, so sperm can't get from the testis to the outside,

32
00:01:54.972 --> 00:01:59.226
though fluid from the seminal vesicles and the prostate still leaves.

33
00:01:59.676 --> 00:02:04.086
The seminal vesicles: paired glands on the back wall of the bladder.

34
00:02:04.086 --> 00:02:07.977
Each one joins its vas deferens to form an ejaculatory duct.

35
00:02:07.977 --> 00:02:12.517
They make about sixty per cent of the semen: a sticky, alkaline fluid,

36
00:02:12.517 --> 00:02:15.889
with fructose to feed the sperm, and prostaglandins.

37
00:02:16.339 --> 00:02:21.940
The prostate: a doughnut-shaped gland under the bladder, wrapped around the urethra.

38
00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:27.741
It adds about a third of the semen: a milky fluid with citric acid as an energy source,

39
00:02:27.741 --> 00:02:30.675
enzymes, and prostate-specific antigen, PSA.

40
00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:37.296
The bulbourethral glands, also called Cowper's glands: pea-sized, just below the prostate.

41
00:02:37.296 --> 00:02:40.039
Before ejaculation they release a thick,

42
00:02:40.039 --> 00:02:44.907
clear mucus that neutralises any traces of acidic urine in the urethra.

43
00:02:46.357 --> 00:02:51.939
The urethra: it carries both urine and semen, at different times, through the one opening.

44
00:02:51.939 --> 00:02:57.336
It has three parts: prostatic, through the prostate; membranous; and spongy, or penile,

45
00:02:57.336 --> 00:02:58.453
through the penis.

46
00:02:58.903 --> 00:03:03.311
The penis: it delivers the sperm into the female reproductive tract.

47
00:03:03.311 --> 00:03:08.951
It has a root, a shaft, and the glans at the end, covered by the prepuce, the foreskin.

48
00:03:08.951 --> 00:03:14.008
Inside are three columns of erectile tissue: the two corpora cavernosa on top,

49
00:03:14.008 --> 00:03:18.871
and the corpus spongiosum, which surrounds the urethra and forms the glans.

50
00:03:19.321 --> 00:03:24.360
So the path, the way she asks it: testis, epididymis, vas deferens, ampulla,

51
00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:29.134
ejaculatory duct, then the prostatic urethra, and out through the penis.

52
00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:30.248
The traps.

53
00:03:30.248 --> 00:03:33.370
Sperm mature in the epididymis, not the testis.

54
00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:37.223
The dartos is smooth muscle and the cremaster is skeletal:

55
00:03:37.223 --> 00:03:39.946
her quiz offers both the wrong way round.

56
00:03:39.946 --> 00:03:44.197
And the cremaster lifts the testes in the cold, not in the heat.

57
00:03:44.647 --> 00:03:45.245
<v Examiner>Once more.

58
00:03:45.245 --> 00:03:47.634
<v Examiner>The male system, structure by structure.

59
00:03:50.084 --> 00:03:53.199
The scrotum keeps the testes three degrees cooler,

60
00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:57.684
with the dartos wrinkling the skin and the cremaster lifting the testes.

61
00:03:57.684 --> 00:04:03.103
The testes make sperm in the seminiferous tubules and testosterone in the Leydig cells,

62
00:04:03.103 --> 00:04:05.595
and the Sertoli cells nourish the sperm.

63
00:04:05.595 --> 00:04:08.647
The epididymis stores the sperm and matures them.

64
00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:11.451
The vas deferens carries them to the ampulla.

65
00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:15.375
The seminal vesicles add sixty per cent of the semen, alkaline,

66
00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:19.424
with fructose and prostaglandins, and form the ejaculatory ducts.

67
00:04:19.424 --> 00:04:25.031
The prostate, round the urethra under the bladder, adds a third, with citric acid and PSA.

68
00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.771
The bulbourethral glands clear acidic urine.

69
00:04:27.771 --> 00:04:30.948
The urethra carries urine and semen, and the penis,

70
00:04:30.948 --> 00:04:35.247
with its corpora cavernosa and corpus spongiosum, delivers the sperm.
